#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Multiple systems and reduced states"
msgstr "Sistem berbilang dan keadaan teraruh"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we'll turn our attention to how density matrices work for multiple "
"systems, including examples of different types of correlations they can "
"express and how they can be used to describe the states of isolated parts of"
" compound systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kita akan beralih perhatian kepada bagaimana matriks ketumpatan "
"berfungsi untuk sistem berbilang, termasuk contoh-contoh jenis korelasi "
"berbeza yang boleh mereka ungkapkan dan cara mereka boleh digunakan untuk "
"menggambarkan keadaan bahagian terpencil bagi sistem kompaun.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Multiple systems {#multiple-systems}"
msgstr "Sistem berbilang {#multiple-systems}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Density matrices can represent states of multiple systems in an analogous way to state vectors in the simplified formulation of quantum information, following the same basic idea that multiple systems can be viewed as if they're single, compound systems.\n"
"In mathematical terms, the rows and columns of density matrices representing states of multiple systems are placed in correspondence with the Cartesian product of the classical state sets of the individual systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Matriks ketumpatan boleh mewakili keadaan sistem berbilang dengan cara yang serupa dengan vektor keadaan dalam formulasi ringkas maklumat kuantum, mengikut idea asas yang sama bahawa sistem berbilang boleh dilihat seolah-olah ia adalah sistem tunggal yang kompaun.\n"
"Dari segi matematik, baris dan lajur matriks ketumpatan yang mewakili keadaan sistem berbilang ditempatkan dalam perkaitan dengan hasil darab Cartesian bagi set keadaan klasik sistem-sistem individu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, recall the state vector representations of the four Bell "
"states.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh, ingat kembali perwakilan vektor keadaan bagi empat keadaan "
"Bell.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 01 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 10 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 01 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 10 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 01 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 10 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 01 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 10 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The density matrix representations of these states are as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perwakilan matriks ketumpatan bagi keadaan-keadaan ini adalah seperti "
"berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\langle \\phi^+ \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\langle \\phi^+ \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi^- \\rangle \\langle \\phi^- \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  -\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi^- \\rangle \\langle \\phi^- \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  -\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi^+ \\rangle \\langle \\psi^+ \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi^+ \\rangle \\langle \\psi^+ \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi^- \\rangle \\langle \\psi^- \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi^- \\rangle \\langle \\psi^- \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Product states {#product-states}"
msgstr "Keadaan hasil darab {#product-states}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Similar to what we had for state vectors, tensor products of density matrices represent *independence* between the states of multiple systems.\n"
"For instance, if $\\mathsf{X}$ is prepared in the state represented by the density matrix $\\rho$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ is independently prepared in the state represented by $\\sigma,$ then the density matrix describing the state of $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ is the tensor product $\\rho\\otimes\\sigma.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sama seperti yang kita ada untuk vektor keadaan, hasil darab tensor matriks ketumpatan mewakili *kebebasan* antara keadaan sistem berbilang.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, jika $\\mathsf{X}$ disediakan dalam keadaan yang diwakili oleh matriks ketumpatan $\\rho$ dan $\\mathsf{Y}$ disediakan secara bebas dalam keadaan yang diwakili oleh $\\sigma,$ maka matriks ketumpatan yang menggambarkan keadaan $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ ialah hasil darab tensor $\\rho\\otimes\\sigma.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The same terminology is used here as in the simplified formulation of "
"quantum information: states of this form are referred to as *product "
"states*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Terminologi yang sama digunakan di sini seperti dalam formulasi ringkas "
"maklumat kuantum: keadaan yang berbentuk ini dirujuk sebagai *keadaan hasil "
"darab*.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Correlated and entangled states {#correlated-and-entangled-states}"
msgstr "Keadaan berkorelasi dan terbelit {#correlated-and-entangled-states}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"States that cannot be expressed as product states represent *correlations* between systems.\n"
"There are, in fact, different types of correlations that can be represented by density matrices.\n"
"Here are a few examples.\n"
msgstr ""
"Keadaan yang tidak boleh dinyatakan sebagai keadaan hasil darab mewakili *korelasi* antara sistem-sistem.\n"
"Sebenarnya, terdapat jenis-jenis korelasi berbeza yang boleh diwakili oleh matriks ketumpatan.\n"
"Berikut ialah beberapa contoh.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Correlated classical states.*\n"
"For example, we can express the situation in which Alice and Bob share a random bit like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"*Keadaan klasik berkorelasi.*\n"
"Sebagai contoh, kita boleh menyatakan situasi di mana Alice dan Bob berkongsi bit rawak seperti ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert +\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\n"
"   =\n"
"   \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"   \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert +\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\n"
"   =\n"
"   \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"   \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Ensembles of quantum states.*\n"
"Suppose we have $m$ density matrices $\\rho_0,\\ldots,\\rho_{m-1},$ all representing states of a system $\\mathsf{X},$ and we  randomly choose one of these states according to a probability vector $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{m-1}).$ Such a process is represented by an *ensemble* of states, which includes the specification of the density matrices $\\rho_0,\\ldots,\\rho_{m-1},$ as well as the probabilities $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{m-1}).$ We can associate an ensemble of states with a single density matrix, describing both the random choice of $k$ and the corresponding density matrix $\\rho_k,$ like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"*Ensembel keadaan kuantum.*\n"
"Andaikan kita mempunyai $m$ matriks ketumpatan $\\rho_0,\\ldots,\\rho_{m-1},$ semuanya mewakili keadaan sistem $\\mathsf{X},$ dan kita memilih secara rawak salah satu keadaan ini mengikut vektor kebarangkalian $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{m-1}).$ Proses sedemikian diwakili oleh sebuah *ensembel* keadaan, yang merangkumi spesifikasi matriks ketumpatan $\\rho_0,\\ldots,\\rho_{m-1},$ serta kebarangkalian $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{m-1}).$ Kita boleh mengaitkan ensembel keadaan dengan matriks ketumpatan tunggal, yang menggambarkan kedua-dua pilihan rawak $k$ dan matriks ketumpatan yang sepadan $\\rho_k,$ seperti ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\vert k\\rangle \\langle k \\vert \\otimes \\rho_k.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\vert k\\rangle \\langle k \\vert \\otimes \\rho_k.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   To be clear, this is the state of a pair $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ "
"where $\\mathsf{Y}$ represents the classical selection of $k$ — so we're "
"assuming its classical state set is $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}.$ States of this "
"form are sometimes called *classical-quantum states*.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Untuk menjelaskan, ini adalah keadaan pasangan "
"$(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ di mana $\\mathsf{Y}$ mewakili pemilihan klasik "
"$k$ — jadi kita menganggap set keadaan klasiknya ialah "
"$\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}.$ Keadaan berbentuk ini kadang-kadang dipanggil "
"*keadaan klasik-kuantum*.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Separable states*. We can imagine situations in which we have a classical "
"correlation among the quantum states of two systems like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"*Keadaan boleh-pisah*. Kita boleh bayangkan situasi di mana terdapat "
"korelasi klasik antara keadaan kuantum dua sistem seperti ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\rho_k \\otimes \\sigma_k.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\rho_k \\otimes \\sigma_k.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   In words, for each $k$ from $0$ to $m-1,$ we have that with probability "
"$p_k$ the system on the left is in the state $\\rho_k$ and the system on the"
" right is in the state $\\sigma_k.$ States like this are called *separable "
"states*. This concept can also be extended to more than two systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Dengan kata-kata, bagi setiap $k$ dari $0$ hingga $m-1,$ kita mempunyai "
"bahawa dengan kebarangkalian $p_k$ sistem di sebelah kiri berada dalam "
"keadaan $\\rho_k$ dan sistem di sebelah kanan berada dalam keadaan "
"$\\sigma_k.$ Keadaan seperti ini dipanggil *keadaan boleh-pisah*. Konsep ini"
" juga boleh dilanjutkan kepada lebih daripada dua sistem.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Entangled states*. Not all states of pairs of systems are separable. In the"
" general formulation of quantum information, this is how entanglement is "
"defined: states that are not separable are said to be *entangled*.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Keadaan terbelit*. Tidak semua keadaan pasangan sistem boleh dipisahkan. "
"Dalam formulasi umum maklumat kuantum, inilah cara keterbelitan ditakrifkan:"
" keadaan yang tidak boleh dipisahkan dikatakan *terbelit*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Note that this terminology is consistent with the terminology we used in "
"the \"Basics of quantum information\" course. There we said that quantum "
"state vectors that are not product states represent entangled states — and "
"indeed, for any quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ that is not a "
"product state, we find that the state represented by the density matrix "
"$\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert$ is not separable. Entanglement is "
"much more complicated than this for states that are not pure.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Perhatikan bahawa terminologi ini adalah konsisten dengan terminologi "
"yang kita gunakan dalam kursus \"Asas maklumat kuantum\". Di sana kita "
"mengatakan bahawa vektor keadaan kuantum yang bukan keadaan hasil darab "
"mewakili keadaan terbelit — dan memang benar, bagi mana-mana vektor keadaan "
"kuantum $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ yang bukan keadaan hasil darab, kita mendapati"
" bahawa keadaan yang diwakili oleh matriks ketumpatan "
"$\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert$ tidak boleh dipisahkan. "
"Keterbelitan jauh lebih rumit daripada ini untuk keadaan yang bukan tulen.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Reduced states and the partial trace {#reduced-states-and-the-partial-trace}"
msgstr ""
"Keadaan teraruh dan surih separa {#reduced-states-and-the-partial-trace}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There's a simple but important thing we can do with density matrices in the context of multiple systems, which is to describe the states we obtain by ignoring some of the systems.\n"
"When multiple systems are in a quantum state and we discard or choose to ignore one or more of the systems,\n"
"the state of the remaining systems is called the *reduced state* of those systems.\n"
"Density matrix descriptions of reduced states are easily obtained through a mapping, known as the *partial trace*, from the density matrix describing the state of the whole.\n"
msgstr ""
"Terdapat perkara mudah tetapi penting yang boleh kita lakukan dengan matriks ketumpatan dalam konteks sistem berbilang, iaitu menggambarkan keadaan yang kita peroleh dengan mengabaikan sebahagian sistem.\n"
"Apabila sistem berbilang berada dalam keadaan kuantum dan kita membuang atau memilih untuk mengabaikan satu atau lebih sistem,\n"
"keadaan sistem yang tinggal dipanggil *keadaan teraruh* sistem-sistem tersebut.\n"
"Penerangan matriks ketumpatan bagi keadaan teraruh boleh diperoleh dengan mudah melalui pemetaan yang dikenali sebagai *surih separa*, daripada matriks ketumpatan yang menggambarkan keadaan keseluruhan.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Example: reduced states for an e-bit {#example-reduced-states-for-an-e-bit}"
msgstr ""
"Contoh: keadaan teraruh bagi e-bit {#example-reduced-states-for-an-e-bit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that we have a pair of qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ that are "
"together in the state\n"
msgstr ""
"Andaikan kita mempunyai sepasang qubit $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ yang "
"bersama-sama berada dalam keadaan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can imagine that Alice holds the qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ and Bob holds $\\mathsf{B},$ which is to say that together they share an e-bit.\n"
"We'd like to have a density matrix description of Alice's qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ in isolation, as if Bob decided to take his qubit and visit the stars, never to be seen again.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita boleh bayangkan Alice memegang qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ dan Bob memegang $\\mathsf{B},$ yakni mereka bersama-sama berkongsi sebuah e-bit.\n"
"Kita ingin mempunyai penerangan matriks ketumpatan bagi qubit Alice $\\mathsf{A}$ secara terpencil, seolah-olah Bob memutuskan untuk membawa qubit-nya dan melawat bintang-bintang, tidak pernah kelihatan lagi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First let's think about what would happen if Bob decided somewhere on his journey to measure his qubit with respect to a standard basis measurement.\n"
"If he did this, he would obtain the outcome $0$ with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, mari kita fikirkan apa yang akan berlaku jika Bob memutuskan di suatu tempat dalam perjalanannya untuk mengukur qubit-nya dengan pengukuran asas piawai.\n"
"Jika dia berbuat demikian, dia akan memperoleh hasil $0$ dengan kebarangkalian\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle 0\\vert \\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2\n"
"= \\Bigl\\| \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\Bigr\\|^2 = \\frac{1}{2},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle 0\\vert \\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2\n"
"= \\Bigl\\| \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\Bigr\\|^2 = \\frac{1}{2},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"in which case the state of Alice's qubit becomes $\\vert 0\\rangle;$ and he "
"would obtain the outcome $1$ with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"dalam kes itu keadaan qubit Alice menjadi $\\vert 0\\rangle;$ dan dia akan "
"memperoleh hasil $1$ dengan kebarangkalian\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle 1\\vert \\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2\n"
"= \\Bigl\\| \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\Bigr\\|^2 = \\frac{1}{2},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle 1\\vert \\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2\n"
"= \\Bigl\\| \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\Bigr\\|^2 = \\frac{1}{2},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "in which case the state of Alice's qubit becomes $\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr "dalam kes itu keadaan qubit Alice menjadi $\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, if we ignore Bob's measurement outcome and focus on Alice's qubit, we conclude that she obtains the state $\\vert 0\\rangle$ with probability $1/2$ and the state $\\vert 1\\rangle$ with probability $1/2.$\n"
"This leads us to describe the state of Alice's qubit in isolation by the density matrix\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadi, jika kita mengabaikan hasil pengukuran Bob dan fokus pada qubit Alice, kita menyimpulkan bahawa dia memperoleh keadaan $\\vert 0\\rangle$ dengan kebarangkalian $1/2$ dan keadaan $\\vert 1\\rangle$ dengan kebarangkalian $1/2.$\n"
"Ini membawa kita untuk menggambarkan keadaan qubit Alice secara terpencil dengan matriks ketumpatan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert = \\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert = \\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That is, Alice's qubit is in the completely mixed state.\n"
"To be clear, this description of the state of Alice's qubit doesn't include Bob's measurement outcome; we're ignoring Bob altogether.\n"
msgstr ""
"Yakni, qubit Alice berada dalam keadaan bercampur sepenuhnya.\n"
"Untuk menjelaskan, penerangan keadaan qubit Alice secara terpencil yang baru kita peroleh tidak termasuk hasil pengukuran Bob; kita mengabaikan Bob sepenuhnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, it might seem like the density matrix description of Alice's qubit in isolation that we've just obtained relies on the assumption that Bob has measured his qubit, but this is not actually so.\n"
"What we've done is to use the possibility that Bob measures his qubit to argue that the completely mixed state arises as the state of Alice's qubit, based on what we've already learned.\n"
"Of course, nothing says that Bob must measure his qubit — but nothing says that he doesn't.\n"
"And if he's light years away, then nothing he does or doesn't do can possibly influence the state of Alice's qubit viewed it in isolation.\n"
"That is to say, the description we've obtained for the state of Alice's qubit is the only description consistent with the impossibility of faster-than-light communication.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang, mungkin nampak seperti penerangan matriks ketumpatan qubit Alice secara terpencil yang baru kita peroleh bergantung pada andaian bahawa Bob telah mengukur qubit-nya, tetapi sebenarnya tidak begitu.\n"
"Apa yang kita lakukan ialah menggunakan kemungkinan bahawa Bob mengukur qubit-nya untuk menyatakan bahawa keadaan bercampur sepenuhnya timbul sebagai keadaan qubit Alice, berdasarkan apa yang telah kita pelajari.\n"
"Sudah tentu, tiada yang menyatakan Bob mesti mengukur qubit-nya — tetapi tiada juga yang menyatakan dia tidak.\n"
"Dan jika dia berada berjuta-juta tahun cahaya jauhnya, maka apa yang dilakukannya atau tidak dilakukannya tidak mungkin mempengaruhi keadaan qubit Alice jika dilihat secara terpencil.\n"
"Dengan kata lain, penerangan yang kita peroleh bagi keadaan qubit Alice adalah satu-satunya penerangan yang konsisten dengan ketidakmungkinan komunikasi lebih pantas daripada cahaya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also consider the state of Bob's qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ which happens to be the completely mixed state as well.\n"
"Indeed, for all four Bell states we find that the reduced state of both Alice's qubit and Bob's qubit is the completely mixed state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita juga boleh mempertimbangkan keadaan qubit Bob $\\mathsf{B},$ yang kebetulan juga merupakan keadaan bercampur sepenuhnya.\n"
"Memang, bagi keempat-empat keadaan Bell kita mendapati bahawa keadaan teraruh kedua-dua qubit Alice dan qubit Bob ialah keadaan bercampur sepenuhnya.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Reduced states for a general quantum state vector {#reduced-states-for-a-"
"general-quantum-state-vector}"
msgstr ""
"Keadaan teraruh bagi vektor keadaan kuantum umum {#reduced-states-for-a-"
"general-quantum-state-vector}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's generalize the example just discussed to two arbitrary systems $\\mathsf{A}$ and $\\mathsf{B},$ not necessarily qubits in the state $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle.$\n"
"We'll assume the classical state sets of $\\mathsf{A}$ and $\\mathsf{B}$ are $\\Sigma$ and $\\Gamma,$ respectively.\n"
"A density matrix $\\rho$ representing a state of the combined system $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ therefore has row and column indices corresponding to the Cartesian product $\\Sigma\\times\\Gamma.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang mari kita umumkan contoh yang baru dibincangkan kepada dua sistem sewenang-wenangnya $\\mathsf{A}$ dan $\\mathsf{B},$ tidak semestinya qubit dalam keadaan $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle.$\n"
"Kita akan menganggap set keadaan klasik $\\mathsf{A}$ dan $\\mathsf{B}$ masing-masing ialah $\\Sigma$ dan $\\Gamma.$\n"
"Matriks ketumpatan $\\rho$ yang mewakili keadaan sistem gabungan $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ oleh itu mempunyai indeks baris dan lajur yang sepadan dengan hasil darab Cartesian $\\Sigma\\times\\Gamma.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that the state of $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ is described by the quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ so the density matrix describing this state is $\\rho = \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert.$\n"
"We'll obtain a density matrix description of the state of $\\mathsf{A}$ in isolation, which is conventionally denoted $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}.$\n"
"(A superscript is also sometimes used rather than a subscript.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Andaikan keadaan $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ digambarkan oleh vektor keadaan kuantum $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ jadi matriks ketumpatan yang menggambarkan keadaan ini ialah $\\rho = \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert.$\n"
"Kita akan memperoleh penerangan matriks ketumpatan bagi keadaan $\\mathsf{A}$ secara terpencil, yang secara konvensional ditulis sebagai $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}.$\n"
"(Superskrip kadang-kadang juga digunakan dan bukannya subskrip.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ can be expressed in the form\n"
msgstr "Vektor keadaan $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ boleh dinyatakan dalam bentuk\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\vert\\phi_b\\rangle \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\vert\\phi_b\\rangle \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for a uniquely determined collection of vectors $\\{\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle : b\\in\\Gamma\\}.$\n"
"In particular, these vectors can be determined through a simple formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"bagi suatu koleksi vektor $\\{\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle : b\\in\\Gamma\\}$ yang ditentukan secara unik.\n"
"Khususnya, vektor-vektor ini boleh ditentukan melalui formula ringkas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle = \\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr)\\vert\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle = \\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr)\\vert\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Reasoning similarly to the previous example of an e-bit, if we were to "
"measure the system $\\mathsf{B}$ with a standard basis measurement, we would"
" obtain each outcome $b\\in\\Gamma$ with probability "
"$\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2,$ in which case the state of $\\mathsf{A}$ "
"becomes\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan membuat alasan serupa dengan contoh e-bit sebelumnya, jika kita "
"mengukur sistem $\\mathsf{B}$ dengan pengukuran asas piawai, kita akan "
"memperoleh setiap hasil $b\\in\\Gamma$ dengan kebarangkalian "
"$\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2,$ dalam kes itu keadaan $\\mathsf{A}$ "
"menjadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "As a density matrix, this state can be written as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai matriks ketumpatan, keadaan ini boleh ditulis seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\biggl(\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}\\biggr)\n"
"\\biggl(\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}\\biggr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\biggl(\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}\\biggr)\n"
"\\biggl(\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}\\biggr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Averaging the different states according to the probabilities of the "
"respective outcomes, we arrive at the density matrix\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan merata-ratakan keadaan-keadaan berbeza mengikut kebarangkalian hasil "
"yang masing-masing, kita tiba pada matriks ketumpatan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2 \\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2}\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr) \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2 \\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2}\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr) \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The partial trace {#the-partial-trace}"
msgstr "Surih separa {#the-partial-trace}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The formula\n"
msgstr "Formula\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"leads us to the description of the reduced state of $\\mathsf{A}$ for any "
"density matrix $\\rho$ of the pair $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ not just a "
"pure state.\n"
msgstr ""
"membawa kita kepada penerangan keadaan teraruh $\\mathsf{A}$ bagi mana-mana "
"matriks ketumpatan $\\rho$ pasangan $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ bukan hanya"
" keadaan tulen.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This formula must work, simply by linearity together with the fact that "
"every density matrix can be written as a convex combination of pure "
"states.\n"
msgstr ""
"Formula ini mesti berfungsi, semata-mata berdasarkan lineariti bersama-sama "
"dengan fakta bahawa setiap matriks ketumpatan boleh ditulis sebagai "
"kombinasi cembung keadaan-keadaan tulen.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The operation being performed on $\\rho$ to obtain $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ in this equation is known as the *partial trace*, and to be more precise we say that the partial trace is performed on $\\mathsf{B},$ or that $\\mathsf{B}$ is *traced out*.\n"
"This operation is denoted $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}},$ so we can write\n"
msgstr ""
"Operasi yang dilakukan pada $\\rho$ untuk memperoleh $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ dalam persamaan ini dikenali sebagai *surih separa*, dan lebih tepat lagi kita katakan surih separa dilakukan pada $\\mathsf{B},$ atau bahawa $\\mathsf{B}$ *disurih keluar*.\n"
"Operasi ini ditulis sebagai $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}},$ jadi kita boleh tulis\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}} (\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}} (\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also define the partial trace on $\\mathsf{A},$ so it's the system "
"$\\mathsf{A}$ that gets traced out rather than $\\mathsf{B},$ like this.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita juga boleh mentakrifkan surih separa pada $\\mathsf{A},$ supaya ia "
"adalah sistem $\\mathsf{A}$ yang disurih keluar dan bukannya $\\mathsf{B},$ "
"seperti ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}} (\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\langle a \\vert\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl(\\vert a \\rangle\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}} (\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\langle a \\vert\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl(\\vert a \\rangle\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This gives us the density matrix description $\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ of the "
"state of $\\mathsf{B}$ in isolation rather than $\\mathsf{A}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini memberi kita penerangan matriks ketumpatan $\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ bagi "
"keadaan $\\mathsf{B}$ secara terpencil dan bukannya $\\mathsf{A}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To recapitulate, if $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ is any pair of systems and "
"we have a density matrix $\\rho$ describing a state of "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ the *reduced states* of the systems "
"$\\mathsf{A}$ and $\\mathsf{B}$ are as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk merumuskan semula, jika $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ ialah mana-mana "
"pasangan sistem dan kita mempunyai matriks ketumpatan $\\rho$ yang "
"menggambarkan keadaan $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ *keadaan teraruh* sistem "
"$\\mathsf{A}$ dan $\\mathsf{B}$ adalah seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho)\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr) \\rho \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\vert a \\rangle\\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}} \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho)\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr) \\rho \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\vert a \\rangle\\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}} \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $\\rho$ is a density matrix, then $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ and "
"$\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ will also necessarily be density matrices.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika $\\rho$ ialah matriks ketumpatan, maka $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ dan "
"$\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ juga semestinya akan menjadi matriks ketumpatan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These notions can be generalized to any number of systems in place of two in a natural way.\n"
"In general, we can put the names of whatever systems we choose in the subscript of a density matrix $\\rho$ to describe the reduced state of just those systems.\n"
"For example, if $\\mathsf{A},$ $\\mathsf{B},$ and $\\mathsf{C}$ are systems and $\\rho$ is a density matrix describing a state of $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{C}),$ then we can define\n"
msgstr ""
"Gagasan-gagasan ini boleh diumumkan kepada sebarang bilangan sistem menggantikan dua dalam cara yang semula jadi.\n"
"Secara umum, kita boleh meletakkan nama-nama mana-mana sistem yang kita pilih dalam subskrip matriks ketumpatan $\\rho$ untuk menggambarkan keadaan teraruh sistem-sistem tersebut sahaja.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, jika $\\mathsf{A},$ $\\mathsf{B},$ dan $\\mathsf{C}$ adalah sistem-sistem dan $\\rho$ ialah matriks ketumpatan yang menggambarkan keadaan $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{C}),$ maka kita boleh takrifkan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{AC}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{C}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{AB}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\vert a \\rangle \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{AC}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{C}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{AB}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\vert a \\rangle \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and similarly for other choices for the systems.\n"
msgstr "dan begitu juga untuk pilihan-pilihan lain sistem.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alternative description of the partial trace {#alternative-description-of-"
"the-partial-trace}"
msgstr ""
"Penerangan alternatif untuk surih separa {#alternative-description-of-the-"
"partial-trace}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An alternative way to describe the partial trace mappings "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}$ and $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}$ is"
" that they are the *unique* linear mappings that satisfy the formulas\n"
msgstr ""
"Cara lain untuk menerangkan pemetaan surih separa "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}$ dan $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}$ "
"ialah ia merupakan pemetaan linear *unik* yang memenuhi formula berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(M \\otimes N) & = \\operatorname{Tr}(M) N \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(M \\otimes N) & = \\operatorname{Tr}(N) M.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(M \\otimes N) & = \\operatorname{Tr}(M) N \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(M \\otimes N) & = \\operatorname{Tr}(N) M.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In these formulas, $N$ and $M$ are square matrices of the appropriate sizes:\n"
"the rows and columns of $M$ correspond to the classical states of $\\mathsf{A}$ and the rows and columns of $N$ correspond to the classical states of $\\mathsf{B}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam formula-formula ini, $N$ dan $M$ ialah matriks persegi dengan saiz yang sesuai:\n"
"baris dan lajur $M$ berpadanan dengan keadaan klasik $\\mathsf{A}$ manakala baris dan lajur $N$ berpadanan dengan keadaan klasik $\\mathsf{B}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This characterization of the partial trace is not only fundamental from a mathematical viewpoint, but can also allow for quick calculations in some situations.\n"
"For example, consider this state of a pair of qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Pencirian surih separa ini bukan sahaja penting dari sudut pandang matematik, malah ia juga boleh mempercepatkan pengiraan dalam situasi-situasi tertentu.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, perhatikan keadaan pasangan qubit $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert \\otimes \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert \\otimes \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To compute the reduced state $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ for instance, we can use linearity together with the fact that\n"
"$\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert$ and $\\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert$ have unit trace.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mengira keadaan teraruh $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ misalnya, kita boleh menggunakan sifat linear bersama fakta bahawa\n"
"$\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert$ dan $\\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert$ mempunyai surih bernilai satu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert\\bigr)\\, \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert  +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\\bigr) \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert\\bigr)\\, \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert  +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\\bigr) \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The reduced state $\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ can be computed similarly.\n"
msgstr "Keadaan teraruh $\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ boleh dikira dengan cara yang sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}} =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert\\bigr)\\, \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert  +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\\bigr) \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}} =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert\\bigr)\\, \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert  +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\\bigr) \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The partial trace for two qubits {#the-partial-trace-for-two-qubits}"
msgstr "Surih separa untuk dua qubit {#the-partial-trace-for-two-qubits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The partial trace can also be described explicitly in terms of matrices.\n"
"Here we'll do this just for two qubits, but this can also be generalized to larger systems.\n"
"Assume that we have two qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ so that any density matrix describing a state of these two qubits can be written as\n"
msgstr ""
"Surih separa juga boleh diterangkan secara eksplisit dalam bentuk matriks.\n"
"Di sini kita akan lakukan ini hanya untuk dua qubit, tetapi cara ini boleh digeneralisasikan kepada sistem yang lebih besar.\n"
"Andaikan kita mempunyai dua qubit $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ supaya sebarang matriks ketumpatan yang menerangkan keadaan dua qubit ini boleh ditulis sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for some choice of complex numbers $\\{\\alpha_{jk} : 0\\leq j,k\\leq 3\\}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"untuk sesetengah pilihan nombor kompleks $\\{\\alpha_{jk} : 0\\leq j,k\\leq "
"3\\}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The partial trace over the first system has the following formula.\n"
msgstr "Surih separa ke atas sistem pertama mempunyai formula berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} +\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} + \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{01} + \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} + \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{11} + \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} +\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} + \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{01} + \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} + \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{11} + \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One way to think about this formula begins by viewing $4\\times 4$ matrices as $2\\times 2$ block matrices, where each block is $2\\times 2.$\n"
"That is,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Salah satu cara untuk memahami formula ini bermula dengan memandang matriks $4\\times 4$ sebagai matriks blok $2\\times 2$, di mana setiap blok bersaiz $2\\times 2.$\n"
"Iaitu,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for\n"
msgstr "untuk\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M_{0,0} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{0,1} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{1,0} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{1,1} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M_{0,0} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{0,1} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{1,0} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{1,1} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We then have\n"
msgstr "Kita kemudiannya mendapat\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= M_{0,0} + M_{1,1}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= M_{0,0} + M_{1,1}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's the formula when the second system is traced out rather than the "
"first.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut pula adalah formula apabila sistem kedua yang disurih keluar dan "
"bukan sistem pertama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} + \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{02} + \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} + \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{22} + \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} + \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{02} + \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} + \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{22} + \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In terms of block matrices of a form similar to before, we have this "
"formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam bentuk matriks blok yang serupa seperti sebelum ini, kita mempunyai "
"formula ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(M_{0,0}) & \\operatorname{Tr}(M_{0,1}) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(M_{1,0}) & \\operatorname{Tr}(M_{1,1})\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(M_{0,0}) & \\operatorname{Tr}(M_{0,1}) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(M_{1,0}) & \\operatorname{Tr}(M_{1,1})\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The block matrix descriptions of these functions can be extended to systems "
"larger than qubits in a natural and direct way.\n"
msgstr ""
"Penerangan matriks blok bagi fungsi-fungsi ini boleh dilanjutkan kepada "
"sistem yang lebih besar daripada qubit dengan cara yang semula jadi dan "
"langsung.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To finish the lesson, let's apply these formulas to the same state we "
"considered above.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mengakhiri pelajaran, mari kita terapkan formula-formula ini pada "
"keadaan yang sama yang kita pertimbangkan di atas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\otimes \\vert +\\rangle \\langle + \\vert\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\otimes \\vert +\\rangle \\langle + \\vert\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The reduced state of the first system $\\mathsf{A}$ is\n"
msgstr "Keadaan teraruh sistem pertama $\\mathsf{A}$ ialah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and the reduced state of the second system $\\mathsf{B}$ is\n"
msgstr "dan keadaan teraruh sistem kedua $\\mathsf{B}$ ialah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"+\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
